<PolicyLayout
  title="Editorial Independence | Miami Debt Help"
  description="Miami Debt Help's editorial independence policy — who can pay for placement, what that payment affects, how listings are verified regardless of payment, and how to challenge inaccurate information."
  lang="en"
  altLangPath="/es/editorial-independence/"
  breadcrumbLabel="Editorial Independence"
  h1="Editorial Independence"
  intro="A trust page is only worth something if it's specific enough to be checked. This one is: who can pay, what that buys, and what stays completely separate from payment."
>
  <h2>Who can pay for placement</h2>
  <p>
    Any organization in one of our listed categories — nonprofit credit counseling, bankruptcy
    attorneys, legal aid, credit unions, housing counselors — can request a featured placement,
    whether or not it's a nonprofit. Payment is never a substitute for meeting the same
    verification standard applied to every listing; an organization that doesn't pass
    verification isn't listed, paid or not.
  </p>

  <h2>What payment changes</h2>
  <p>
    A featured placement and its badge. That's the entire scope of what payment affects on this
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>What payment never changes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Whether an organization is verified, and what specifically was or wasn't confirmed
      about it.</li>
    <li>Whether nonprofit, free options appear before paid ones on the page.</li>
    <li>The wording used to describe what an organization does — no promotional language, no
      unverified superlatives, regardless of who's paying.</li>
    <li>How quickly a reported error about a listing gets corrected.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How a provider can challenge inaccurate information</h2>
  <p>
    Any organization — listed or not, paid or not — can flag something inaccurate about how
    it's described on this site through the same public <a href="/report-an-error/">Report an
    Error</a> process available to every reader. A correction is evaluated against the same
    source-tiering standard described in <a href="/how-we-verify/">How We Verify</a>, not
    granted automatically because a business requested it, and not withheld because it happens
    to be a paying listing.
  </p>

  <h2>Review cadence</h2>
  <p>
    Listings are re-checked on a set schedule, not published once and left alone — each listing
    carries a last-verified date. Paid status doesn't change the review schedule in either
    direction.
  </p>

  <h2>See also</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="/how-we-make-money/">How We Make Money</a> covers where revenue actually comes from.
    This page covers the process guarantees that keep that revenue from touching what gets
    published.
  </p>
</PolicyLayout>
